CONCEPT
  product:  Bias
  one-liner: Rideshare matched on bias alignment, so you are never in a car with someone whose
             ult is wrong.
  angle:    dispatch-desk officialdom applied to fandom taxonomy. The company sincerely treats
            seating compatibility as a transport problem and has staffed for it. Every claim
            carries an unaudited figure, and the appeals process does not exist because in the
            company's view there is nothing to appeal. anti-ai-slop invoked before copy.

DESIGN DIRECTION
  style:    Holographic photocard slab, sealed-sleeve dark mode. The page is staged as a graded
            collectible card sealed in acrylic and photographed on a matte black sleeve. Four
            motifs only: the prismatic foil sweep (fixed-angle gradient on rules, keylines and
            edges, never as a fill under text), the acrylic slab (1px inner keyline plus soft
            outer bloom), the grading label strip (mono serial / population / grade), and the
            matte sleeve field underneath.
  palette:  "Sealed Foil" — primary #7A5BFF (foil violet) / accent #2FE0C2 (foil aqua) /
            bg #08060E (sleeve black) / fg #F1ECFB / muted #9A92B4 / ink #F1ECFB, with
            slab #120E1C and foil stops #7A5BFF #2FE0C2 #FFD66B #FF69C8.
  fonts:    display 'Syncopate' · body 'Manrope' · mono 'Space Mono'
  archetype: on-demand transport booking landing page, run as collectible-grading literature
  anti-sameness check: PASS. Last 7 were vitreous enamel signage (09-18), agricultural equipment
            livery (09-17), pharmaceutical leaflet (09-16), leaded stained glass (09-15),
            risograph zine (09-14), microfilm carrel (09-13), injection-moulded console (09-12).
            No style, font-pair, or palette collision. The nearest palette neighbour is 09-15
            (#2F5FC7 blue on #0D0F16), which is a different hue family and pairs with a red
            accent rather than an aqua one. No violet-on-near-black has appeared in the window,
            and no prior entry has used a multi-stop iridescent gradient as a structural motif.
  skill note: ui-ux-pro-max was invoked and its --design-system pass returned felt-green + gold
            with Inter/Inter, which is the generic dark-SaaS default and was rejected. The font
            pairing was taken from its library instead ("Kinetic Motion", Syncopate + Space Mono,
            filed under music festivals and high-energy brands) and the palette derived custom.
            Its colour library returned 0 results for iridescent/holographic queries.

IMAGES
  budget:   4 of 4 used. GEMINI_API_KEY present, no cap hit, 4 API calls total.
  rationale: Hero taken because the direction is a graded photocard and a photocard is
            definitionally a photograph inside a slab. The 16:9 plate is inset above the h1 so
            it reads as the card's own artwork rather than as a page background, which is work
            no gradient can do. No demo asset generated and none reused: the demo's only
            photo-shaped slots are six driver avatars, the budget cannot cover six, and a
            3-of-6 photo split would read as broken. Reusing the testimonial headshots there
            would also have put the same three faces on the site under two different sets of
            names, so all six drivers take a CSS monogram tile with a lightstick-colour
            underline instead. Remaining 3 slots went to testimonial headshots, one per named
            rider, each on a different palette colour (primary violet, sleeve black with aqua
            rim, slab indigo) so the row reads as three cards pulled from the same set.
  hero.webp        role hero        · 1 attempt · PASS — violet baton spill lands on --primary,
                   the window rim light lands on --accent, cabin blacks sit at --bg. Restrained
                   documentary grade with no golden-hour or neon-cyberpunk tell. Neutral
                   expression reads institutional rather than promotional. No text artifacts.
