BUILD
  landing:  single hero slab on the sleeve field, grading strip (serial / pop / grade 9.5) across
            its top edge, 16:9 photo plate inset, h1 in Syncopate, foil hairline, foil-ringed CTA
            pill. Spec rail of mono figures in the left gutter (4:10 median match, 11 metros,
            612 groups, 0 successful appeals) that collapses to a 3-up row under 900px. Features,
            testimonials and pricing are slab rows; the Ult tier gets the brighter foil edge and
            an accent price. Each pricing slab carries a rider-count grading strip (1,204,882 /
            88,310 / 412), which is the joke and also real information. frontend-design and
            anti-ai-slop both invoked.
  demo:     pre-dispatch driver selection for Night 2 of 3 at a 19,500-seat arena. Sticky surge
            band at 3.8x with its trigger (17-second teaser, 00:00 KST) and a 1.0x-8.0x track.
            Alignment-threshold slider (default 70) filters six driver cards live, each with a
            lightstick-coloured monogram tile, group/bias badges, fandom-entry year, fanchant
            score, barricade distance and a fare recomputed from base × surge + add-ons. Two
            cabin toggles repriced live. Selecting a driver opens a confirm modal that restates
            the alignment score and gates Dispatch behind a mismatch-clause checkbox, with the
            clause text switching by alignment band. Right rail appends a timestamped dispatch
            log per action, capped at 14 lines. Empty state when the threshold clears everybody.
            All vanilla JS, no frameworks, no network calls.

WARNINGS / NEAR-MISSES
  - The hero CTA pill originally drew its foil ring with an absolutely-positioned ::after at
    z-index:-1. Inside a slab that has its own background, the ring would have been painted
    behind the parent and invisible. Rebuilt as a padding-box/border-box gradient border before
    any render. Same construction reused for the demo's Dispatch button.
  - Scroll reveal on the landing page is opacity-only, gated on a .js class with a 1500ms
    timeout fallback and a no-IntersectionObserver early-out, so the page renders identically
    with JS off and cannot photograph blank below the fold. Known trap from a prior run.
  - --primary (#7A5BFF) is roughly 3.7:1 on the slab, so it is used only for large display
    accents, the foil stops and the monogram tiles, never for body text. Body copy runs fg
    (#F1ECFB) and muted (#9A92B4), both comfortably past AA on both --bg and --slab.
  - No slot references a file that does not exist. The demo ships zero <img> tags by design.
  - Gallery rebuilt from all 100 concept.json files, sorted date descending. Header count
    updated to 100. Root metadata contract, favicon link, 50x50 logo lockup, span-wrapped
    slide CTAs, and the carousel nav pattern (arrows, scrollable dot rail with
    scrollIntoView, arrow keys, touch swipe) all preserved and verified programmatically.

VISUAL CHECK (step 9, ran — playwright already present, nothing installed)
  captures: 2 (landing, demo) plus 1 re-capture of the landing after the edit. Within cap.
  fixed 1 real defect with 1 edit:
    1. Section vertical rhythm had collapsed. `section{padding:52px 0}` was being overridden by
       `.wrap{padding:0 var(--gut)}`, because the class selector outranks the bare element
       selector and the shorthand zeroes all four sides. Every section heading was sitting
       roughly 12px below the card row above it. Replaced with `section.wrap{padding-top:64px}`
       at equal specificity. This is the exact CSS-specificity trap the frontend-design skill
       flags, and it was invisible until the screenshot.
  left alone deliberately: the demo's driver rows are tall relative to their content, because
  the right-hand stack (alignment, fare, Select) is three items where the left is two. Airy
  rather than broken, so it is taste and stays.

